# 📱 Camply

> A multi-tenant university engagement platform designed to improve communication between higher education institutions and their students.

![React Native](https://img.shields.io/badge/React_Native-Mobile-blue)
![React](https://img.shields.io/badge/React-Admin_Dashboard-61DAFB)
![Supabase](https://img.shields.io/badge/Supabase-Backend-green)
![Expo](https://img.shields.io/badge/Expo-SDK-black)
![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/Status-MVP-orange)

---

## 📖 Overview

Camply is a Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) platform built to modernize how universities communicate with students.

Many institutions rely on fragmented communication channels such as emails, WhatsApp groups, notice boards, and social media. Important announcements, job opportunities, events, and surveys often fail to reach students effectively.

Camply centralizes these services into a single mobile application while providing administrators with an intuitive dashboard to manage campus communication.

The platform was designed with multi-tenancy in mind, allowing multiple universities to operate independently within the same system.

---

## 🚀 Features

### Student Mobile App

* Secure Authentication
* University-specific access
* View announcements
* Browse upcoming events
* Apply for student job opportunities
* Complete questionnaires and surveys
* Receive real-time notifications
* Modern mobile-first interface

### Admin Dashboard

* Manage university announcements
* Publish events
* Create job opportunities
* Build questionnaires
* View student responses
* Manage university users
* Content management interface

### Super Admin

* Register new universities
* Manage institutions
* Multi-tenant onboarding
* Platform administration

---

## 🏗 Architecture

Camply consists of three main applications:

```text
Camply

├── Student Mobile App (React Native + Expo)
│
├── University Admin Dashboard (React + Vite)
│
└── Backend (Supabase)
      ├── Authentication
      ├── PostgreSQL Database
      ├── Realtime
      ├── Storage
      └── Serverless Functions
```

